    "restrictions": "The datafiles are property of the LISS panel (Centerdata), the core element of the project Measurement and Experimentation in the Social Sciences (MESS), see <a href=\"https://www.lissdata.nl/\">https://www.lissdata.nl/</a>. We are therefore not allowed to redistribute LISS data and only supply our utilized syntax files.",
    "termsOfAccess": "Dear user, \n\nYou are welcome to download the materials of the Dataverse folder entitled “Who cares what other people think? A longitudinal investigation of long-term self-esteem stability and its associations with autonomy-connectedness”, provided you agree with the following conditions: \n\n1. The downloader undertakes to keep confidential any information in the present data concerning individual persons, households, enterprises or institutions which comes to his/her knowledge during the work on the data. \n\n2. They undertake not to distribute materials to others without written permission from L. E. Kunst. \n\n3. They undertake to use the present materials for purely scientific (i.e. non-commercial) research only. \n\n4. They contact at least one of the (co-)authors, in case they want to publish or report on these dataset(s). If appropriate, they agree to include a member of this research group as co-author. \n\n5. They include the following acknowledgement in any publication based on the present dataset(s): In this paper use is made of materials of L. E. Kunst, M. A. L. M. van Assen, F. J. Clouth, C. Hunt, M. Abbott, J. Maas and M. H. J. Bekker. \n\n6. Downloading the materials does not grant exclusivity on the data or the subject. In the situation when proposals with a comparable subject will be submitted, agreement will be sought between the different parties. \n\n7. This statement shall remain valid, even after conclusion of the work of the present data. \n",
    "contactForAccess": "Dr. L. E. Kunst; lauraelenakunst@gmail.com",
